{"seconds": 42.4, "exit": 0, "final": "After Qxc3, White can play bxc3 and Black loses the queen! That's not good. Bxf3 is clearly better because it wins the bishop cleanly.\n\nLet me make sure Bxf3 is indeed the best move and check the main line once more:\n\n**Best Move: Bxf3**\n\nMain line:\n1. ...Bxf3 \n2. gxf3 (or Bxf3) Qxg5+ \n3. Kh2 and Black is up a piece (the g5 bishop is won)\n\n**Motif: fork** (The removal of the f3 knight leaves the g5 bishop undefended and attacked by the queen)\n\n**Coaching Note:**\nWhen your opponent's pieces stop defending each other, strike immediately. White's Bg5 was only safe as long as the Nf3 blocked your bishop. Removing it with Bxf3 forces White into bad recaptures\u2014if gxf3, then Qxg5+ wins the bishop with check; if Bxf3, then Qxg5 wins it cleanly. Always ask: what would happen if that defender moves?\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Bxf3\", \"line\": [\"Bxf3\", \"gxf3\", \"Qxg5+\", \"Kh2\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"deflection\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "e4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "d5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "square": "g4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "move": "Nd5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspe